# The factory reads this file as factory/.env, next to settings.env. It holds secrets, committee ids and host paths, and never leaves its host.
# Every other setting is in settings.env. A key in both files stops the factory. Every key here is required, except BUTLER_API_KEY.
# Folder for the host clone, work clones, logs, state and the inbox.
FACTORY_HOME=
# Folder the web server serves. Builds go to <root>/dev and <root>/<hash>.
FACTORY_WEB_ROOT=
# Address of that folder in a browser, without a trailing slash.
FACTORY_PUBLIC_URL=
# on when the host has an NVIDIA GPU with the container toolkit, as provision sets up. Containers then get the GPU, and the playtest draws on it with its frame rate check.
# off runs the playtest in software, with fewer turns and no frame rate check.
FACTORY_GPU=
# Claude subscription token from `claude setup-token`. It is the only secret agent containers get.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
# The committee lives in $FACTORY_HOME/committee/committee.json and changes with /committee in the chat.
# Until that file exists, the committee is one member: this Telegram user id and GitHub login.
# One committee thumbs-up marks an issue.
FACTORY_COMMITTEE_BOOTSTRAP=
FACTORY_COMMITTEE_BOOTSTRAP_GITHUB=
# Telegram bot shared with Hermes, the committee chat id and the public channel id or @name.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
FACTORY_COMMITTEE_CHAT=
FACTORY_PUBLIC_CHANNEL=
# ElevenLabs key for the game's sfx:gen, which agents may run.
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
# itch.io butler key. Only a release needs it, and it fails loud without it. Only the butler call on the host gets it.
BUTLER_API_KEY=
